  Adiabatic mixing of 36 kmol/h liquid water at 300 K with 36 kmol/h steam at
  450 K, both at 1 bar (IF97).  The summed enthalpy lies inside the saturation
  plateau of water at 1 bar: no temperature carries it (H jumps by the whole
  latent heat at Tsat), so the outlet is T = Tsat(1 bar) = 372.756 K with the
  vapour fraction of the lever rule on the saturated legs (0.4668), taken from
  the pure-fluid plateau route of flashState::specifiedFlash.  Before (D9,
  2026-11-28) the mixer's own inversion in T asked IF97 for 175 K and failed.
  Held: the energy report's mixer remainder (zero) and the mass balance.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

